{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/906836-requiem-for-regina-cruac","id":906836,"title":"Requiem for Regina: Cruac?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-03T17:42:19-07:00","id":906836,"title":"Requiem for Regina: Cruac?","content":"How does one aquire Cruac in the Requiem for Regina setting, when there's no Circle of the Crone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T18:26:47-07:00","id":906868,"title":"","content":"One probably doesn't. It was unheard of at the time and place. Although perhaps you could houserule that a faction like the Dygol Kepen are hoarding such knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 06-03-2016, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T22:33:42-07:00","id":906973,"title":"","content":"By talking to strix, like other non-circle vamps would do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T05:37:46-07:00","id":907069,"title":"","content":"Or joining a bloodline or cult that has a limited form of cruac.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T16:58:19-07:00","id":908720,"title":"","content":"The Veneficia, a forgien sect I believe use Cruac.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T07:06:04-07:00","id":909136,"title":"","content":"I'd be fine with substituting the Covenant Status prerequisite with Mystery Cult Initiation and letting one play a vampire witch with Cruac belonging to one of the myriad covens that later became the Circle. As long as that made any sense for the story I was trying to tell, of course (I try to not limit my players too much, but sometimes it's better to put your foot down than try to fit a square peg through a round hole).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T09:30:53-07:00","id":909223,"title":"","content":"Cruac and Theban Sorcery are not the first or only versions of Blood Magic, they are simply the most common in the modern era. There are probably many 'minor' blood sorceries out there using the Cruac cost of 1 Vitae per ritual dot and a selection of their own rituals, I certainly don't limit Blood Magic to just two/three covenants, although the Carthians and Invictus won't allow them to achieve too much power (mainly to justify only having one or two per city).<br /> <br /> I short, Cruac is essentially generic Blood Magic. Make up some kindred cult, think of a new name for Cruac, and present the idea to your Storyteller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T15:33:20-07:00","id":909522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/906836-requiem-for-regina-cruac?p=908720#post908720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Veneficia, a forgien sect I believe use Cruac.</div> </div> </div> </div>Veneficia was a form of blood magic like Cruac, but less intuitive and more rigidly structured, practiced by ancient Roman vampires. It's described in <i>Requiem for Rome</i>. What's curious is that it's described as something novel to pre-Roman Britain and forgotten since, as opposed to any other type of blood magic besides Theban Sorcery. Now it occurs me to that the Fuil-Beannaithe, another eclectic religious covenant from Ireland, could well have some ability with Cruac, if perhaps not enough to impress the Weihan Cynn, like knowing a handful of rituals so small that it superficially could pass for a weird bloodline discipline. Although it would be interesting to see if they had other tricks up their sleeves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T15:49:09-07:00","id":909540,"title":"","content":"That Shinto Covenant in Japan also has its own verison of Cruac. Sorry thread drift.<br /> <br /> Anyways I don't have Reqiuem for Rome, and RFR is 1e anyways so I'd just use Cruac for Veneficia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T16:51:40-07:00","id":909592,"title":"","content":"Considering the absence of Cruac is a plot point - you don't, at least not as something you just buy with experience via your membership to something. You explore rediscovering it as an in-game plotline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T12:43:41-07:00","id":924569,"title":"","content":"In my game, the Circle was founded around 800 CE, so Cruac is available during Requiem for Regina. I just replaced the Weihan Cynn with the Circle of the Crone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}